The PRE_GetContract method checks the Precondition before the method Get() is invoked. The test case has two input parameters, an array list and an index. The Precondition assumes that the index is within the acceptable range, i.e., greater than or equals to 0 and less than arraylist count. If the index is out of the range, PexAssumeUnderTest will return null or an exception, the method Get() will not be invoked.

In the test method PUT_GetContract() after the method Get() is invoked, the new array list count and the new return value are observed. If the index is out of the range, a NullReferenceException will be raised when Get() is invoked. The test case also checks the return value after the method Get() is invoked. The test case also checks if the new retrieved item is contained within the array list or not.

## Test Case 3: PUT_RemoveContract

```C#
namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        [PexMethod(typeof(ArrayList))]
        public void PUT_RemoveContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, [PexBasicList(4)]object[] listToAdd, int index)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index < arrList.Count && index >= 0);

            int old_count = arrList.Count;

            arrList.AddRange(listToAdd);
            int old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

            int removed_item = (int)arrList[index];
            
            object removed_item_ret = arrList.Remove(removed_item);

            int new_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            bool New_containsRemovedRet = arrList.Contains(removed_item_ret);

            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_count", old_count);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", old_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", new_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$removed_item_ret", removed_item_ret);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_containsRemovedRet", New_containsRemovedRet);

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that @@@ the new arrList count @@@ should be one less than old arrList count

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that @@@ the removed item's return value @@@ should be removed_item's value

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that @@@ after removing item, if it exist in the new arrList, it should not exist in the arrList
        }
    }
}
```

This test case checks the Post condition after the method Remove() is invoked. The test case has 3 input parameters, an array list, a list to add and the index to be removed. The Precondition assumes that the index is within the acceptable range.

In the test method PUT_RemoveContract(), the arrList.AddRange() and arrList.Remove() methods are invoked. Then, the test case observes the old arrList count, new arrList count and the value that is returned by the Remove() method. If the index is out of the range, a NullReferenceException will be raised when Remove() is invoked. The test case also checks whether the removed item is contained within the array list or not.

## Conclusion

This exercise uses Microsoft's PEX to test contracts of ArrayList methods like Add(), Get() and Remove(). By leveraging the PEX tools, we can write various test cases for the contracts to ensure the correct functionality of these methods in an ArrayList. With PEX, the automatic generation of many test cases allows us to efficiently test the entire program code base, including boundary conditions, exceptional--------------------           Debug.Assert(index != Old_arrListCount);

	    // assertion using "Assert.AreEqual\(...\);" that the index element that you retrieved using getter, should be equal to the index itself 
           Assert.AreEqual(New_Ret, Old_index);

	    // Assertion using "Assert.IsTrue\(...\);" that the count after get has stayed the same
           Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount);

	    // Assertion using "Assert.IsTrue\(...\);" that the new retrieved value is present in the list
           Assert.IsTrue(New_containsNewRet);
        }
    }
}
